  "modules": [
    {
      "name": "Atomic",
      "source": "Src/Atomic.rux",
      "header": "A value that threads share without a lock.\n`Atomic<T>` holds one integer of 8 to 64 bits, `bool` or pointer and reaches it only through `Core`'s atomic\nintrinsics, so no thread ever sees a value half written and every change is one indivisible step. The methods take\nthe value by shared reference, because the whole point is that several threads reach it at once; the hardware, not\nthe borrow, is what keeps their accesses apart.\nThe plain methods are sequentially consistent, which is the ordering that is never wrong: every thread agrees on one\norder of all of them. The `With` forms take a weaker `MemoryOrder` for code that has worked out it is enough. The\nintrinsics need their order written as a case, so a `With` method selects among them with a `match`; the plain\nmethods involve no such choice."
    }
  ],
